Here's the Java code implementation of the solution:

```java
import java.util.HashSet;

class Node {
    int value;
    Node next;

    public Node(int value) {
        this.value = value;
        this.next = null;
    }
}

class LinkedList {
    Node head;

    // Other methods and constructors...

    public int getSizeWithoutDuplicates() {
        HashSet<Integer> uniqueValues = new HashSet<>();
        Node currentNode = head;
        while (currentNode != null) {
            uniqueValues.add(currentNode.value);
            currentNode = currentNode.next;
        }
        return uniqueValues.size();
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LinkedList linkedList = new LinkedList();
        linkedList.head = new Node(1);
        linkedList.head.next = new Node(2);
        linkedList.head.next.next = new Node(3);
        linkedList.head.next.next.next = new Node(4);
        linkedList.head.next.next.next.next = new Node(2);
        linkedList.head.next.next.next.next.next = new Node(5);

        int sizeWithoutDuplicates = linkedList.getSizeWithoutDuplicates();
        System.out.println("Size without duplicates: " + sizeWithoutDuplicates);
    }
}
```

