public static boolean isPalindrome(String input) {
    int left = 0;
    int right = input.length() - 1;

    while (left < right) {
        char leftChar = Character.toLowerCase(input.charAt(left));
        char rightChar = Character.toLowerCase(input.charAt(right));

        if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(leftChar)) {
            left++;
        } else if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(rightChar)) {
            right--;
        } else if (leftChar != rightChar) {
            return false;
        } else {
            left++;
            right--;
        }
    }

    return true;
}
```

Explanation:
- The function uses two pointers, `left` and `right`, to iterate through the input string from both ends.
- Inside the while loop, we compare the characters at the current positions of `left` and `right`.
- We use the `Character.toLowerCase()` method to convert both characters to lowercase, making the function case-insensitive.
- We use the `Character.isLetterOrDigit()` method to check if the characters are alphanumeric. If not, we increment the corresponding pointer and continue the loop.
- If both characters are alphanumeric and not equal, we return `false` as the input string is not a palindrome.
- If both characters are alphanumeric and equal, we increment `left` and decrement `right` to move to the next characters.
- The loop continues until `left` becomes greater than or equal to `right`, indicating that we have checked all the necessary pairs of characters.
- If the loop completes without returning `false`, we return `true` as the input string is a palindrome.

This implementation has a time complexity of O(n) and a space complexity of O(1), as it only uses a constant amount of additional space to store the two pointers and temporary characters."}]

