``` java
public static void circularShift(int[] arr) {
    int len = arr.length;
    if (len < 2) {
        return;
    }
    int x = arr[len - 2];
    int y = arr[len - 1];

    for (int i = len - 2; i > 0; i -= 2) {
        arr[i] = arr[i - 2];
        arr[i + 1] = arr[i - 1];
    }

    arr[0] = x;
    arr[1] = y;
}
```
This method first checks if the input array has fewer than 2 elements, as these arrays can be left as they are. Then, it stores the last two elements. Following that, it iterates backwards through the array in steps of 2, moving each pair of elements two positions to the right. Lastly, it starts filling up the first two elements of the array with the last two elements that were stored earlier.

