[{"role": "assistant", "content": "Here is the solution to your problem: A Radix Sort algorithm for sorting hexadecimal numbers in Java. Please note, Java does not support unsigned numbers and it treats hexadecimal numbers as integers. Therefore, the problem of sorting both signed and unsigned numbers can not be addressed consistently in Java.

```Java
import java.util.*;

public class RadixSort {
    private static final int RADIX = 16; // hexadecimal

    public void radixSort(int[] numbers) {
        int maxNumber = Arrays.stream(numbers).max().getAsInt();
        int exp = 1;

        while (maxNumber / exp > 0) {
            countingSort(numbers, exp);
            exp *= RADIX;
        }
    }

    private void countingSort(int[] numbers, int exp) {
        int[] output = new int[numbers.length];

        int[] count = new int[RADIX];
        Arrays.fill(count, 0);

        for (int number : numbers) {
            int digitAtExp = (number/exp) % RADIX;
            count[digitAtExp]++;
        }

        for (int i = 1; i < RADIX; i++) {
            count[i] += count[i - 1];
        }

        for (int i = numbers.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            int digitAtExp = (numbers[i]/exp) % RADIX;
            output[--count[digitAtExp]] = numbers[i];
        }

        System.arraycopy(output, 0, numbers, 0, numbers.length);
    }

    // Test method
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RadixSort rs = new RadixSort();

        int[] numbers = { 0x1F, 0xFF, 0xA, 0x0, 0x2B, 0xAE, 0xB1 };
        rs.radixSort(numbers);

        for (int number : numbers) {
            System.out.format("0x%X ", number);
        }
    }
}
```

This test will print: `0x0 0xA 0x1F 0x2B 0xAE 0xB1 0xFF` which is the sorted list of input hexadecimal numbers. 

Do note that this is a basic Radix Sort that only operates on positive integers. If you want to handle negative integers, you need a different approach and Java does not support unsigned integers. 

If the hexadecimal numbers are stored as strings, you can modify this algorithm to handle them as strings which will also allow handling the signed numbers."}]

