Here are the main points about Constructor:

1. A constructor is invoked at the time of object or instance creation.
2. The constructor must have the same name as the class.
3. Every class has a constructor. If we do not explicitly write one, Java compiler will automatically create it.

Here are the types of constructors:
1. Default constructor: A constructor that doesn’t accept any parameters. It is automatically provided by Java compiler if program does not have any constructors.

