[{"role": "assistant", "content": "Here is a Java method called appendWord that could solve your problem :

You just need to provide sentence, append word, and maximum length. It checks if the sentence after appending exceeds the maximum limit, then it smartly tries to decrease the length by removing some words from the sentence till it fits the maximum length. The smartly removing of word is done by greedy algorithm - removing the longest word first.

```java

import java.util.*;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "Amidst the mists and coldest frosts, with stoutest wrists and loudest boasts, he thrusts his fists against the posts and still insists he sees the ghosts.";
        String append = "Ghost";
        int maxLen = 180;
        System.out.println(appendWord(sentence, append, maxLen));
    }

    public static String appendWord(String sentence, String append, int maxLength) {
        Queue<String> queue = new PriorityQueue<>(Comparator.comparingInt(String::length).reversed());
        String[] words = sentence.split(" ");
        StringBuilder newSentence = new StringBuilder();

        for (String word : words) {
            if (word.endsWith(".") || word.endsWith(",") || word.endsWith("?")) {
                queue.add(word.substring(0, word.length() - 1) + append + word.charAt(word.length() - 1));
            } else {
                queue.add(word + append);
            }
        }

        while (queue.peek() != null) {
            if (newSentence.length() + queue.peek().length() <= maxLength) {
                newSentence.append(queue.poll());
                newSentence.append(" ");
            } else {
                break;
            }
        }

        return newSentence.toString();
    }
}
```
The appendWord method works by splitting sentence into words and then putting them into priority queue with custom comparator that sorts words by their length in descending order. Then it builds new sentence by extracting words from the priority queue and checking if its length after appending word to sentence still not exceeds maxLength. If yes, it appends word to sentence, otherwise does not append and breaks the loop."}]

