            if(isPrime[p] == true)
            {
                // Update all multiples of p
                for(int i = p*p; i < N; i += p)
                    isPrime[i] = false;
            }
        }

        // Displaying the prime numbers smaller than N
        for(int i = 2; i < N; i++)
        {
            if(isPrime[i] == true)
                System.out.println(i + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

Here's how the reasoning process works:

1. We start by assuming all numbers less than N to be prime (boolean array `isPrime[]`).

2. We start from the first prime number, which is 2, iterate through all of its multiples, and mark them as not prime. If `isPrime[p]` is true, then it is a prime.

3. We repeat the step for all numbers up to N.

4. Finally, we iterate over `isPrime[]`, and print all indexes i for which `isPrime[i]` is true. These will be all prime numbers less than N."}]

