public class NelderMeadOptimization {
    public static double[] optimize(Function function, double[] initialParams, double tolerance) {
        NelderMead optimizer = new NelderMead();
        optimizer.setConvergenceTolerance(tolerance);

        Vec initialGuess = new DenseVector(initialParams);
        List<Vec> initialSimplex = new ArrayList<>();
        initialSimplex.add(initialGuess);

        for (int i = 0; i < initialParams.length; i++) {
            double[] perturbedParams = initialParams.clone();
            perturbedParams[i] = perturbedParams[i] + 0.1; // Perturb the parameter
            initialSimplex.add(new DenseVector(perturbedParams));
        }

        Vec solution = optimizer.minimize(function, initialSimplex);
        return solution.arrayCopy();
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `optimize` method initializes the Nelder-Mead optimizer with the given tolerance. It then constructs an initial simplex around the provided initial parameters. The algorithm is used to minimize the given function, and the optimal parameters are returned as an array of doubles."}]

