[{"role": "assistant", "content": "```java
public ListNode reverseKGroup(ListNode head, int k) {
    ListNode curr = head;
    int count = 0;
    while (curr != null && count < k) {
        curr = curr.next;
        count++;
    }
    if (count == k) {
        curr = reverseKGroup(curr, k);
        while (count-- > 0) {
            ListNode temp = head.next;
            head.next = curr;
            curr = head;
            head = temp;
        }
        head = curr;
    }
    return head;
}
```

The `reverseKGroup` function takes the head of the linked list and the integer `k` as input and reverses the nodes of the linked list `k` at a time. If the number of nodes is not a multiple of `k`, then left-out nodes remain as they are. The function uses recursion to reverse the linked list in groups of size `k`."}]

