For example, given the input list ["John", "Jane", "Jim", "Jake"] and a threshold of 2, the method should return ["John - Jane"] since the Levenshtein distance between "John" and "Jane" is 2, which meets the threshold.

Assume that the input list of names will not contain duplicates and will have at least two elements.

